INFO(1)                       Funny CLI Manual                       INFO(1)

NAME
    info — Inspect a filesystem entry and reveal its vital statistics,
           because apparently files have résumés now.

SYNOPSIS
    info <path>

DESCRIPTION
    The 'info' command displays detailed information about a file or
    directory.

    It reports the path, type, size, permissions, modification time,
    and creation/change time.

    In other words, instead of merely asking:

        "What is this?"

    you can now interrogate it properly.

ARGUMENTS
    path
        The file or directory to inspect.

        Required. If omitted, the command provides a usage reminder
        and investigates absolutely nothing.

OUTPUT
    The command displays:

        Path
            The absolute path of the requested entry.

        Type
            Either "Directory" or "File".

        Size
            The size of the entry in human-readable form.

        Permissions
            The filesystem permission bits, formatted in familiar
            Unix-style notation.

        Modified
            The last modification timestamp.

        Created
            The filesystem creation/change timestamp as reported by
            the platform.

    Example:

        Path: /home/user/project
        Type: Directory
        Size: 4.0 KB
        Permissions: drwxr-xr-x
        Modified: 2026-09-03 10:42:17
        Created: 2026-09-01 08:15:03

    Basically, a background check for your files.

ERRORS
    info error: <error>
        Something prevented the command from obtaining information.

        Possible causes include:
        - The path does not exist.
        - Permission denied.
        - The filesystem is feeling secretive.
        - You asked for information about something that has
          mysteriously vanished.

USAGE ERRORS
    > info

        Usage: info <path>

        The command needs someone to investigate.

        You forgot to provide the suspect.

EXAMPLES
    > info README.md
        Displays the file's size, permissions, and timestamps.

        Finally, proof that the README exists.

    > info src
        Displays information about the 'src' directory.

        It's a directory. It has permissions. It has a past.
        It has seen things.

    > info mysterious-file
        info error: ...

        The mystery continues.

    > info .
        Displays information about the current directory.

        The filesystem equivalent of checking your own passport.

FUN FACTS
    - Both files and directories can be inspected.
    - Sizes are displayed using the CLI's human-readable size formatter.
    - Permissions are formatted using Python's filesystem mode
      representation.
    - Timestamps are converted into local datetime values.
    - The command does not modify anything.
    - This may be the safest command in the entire CLI.
    - You can finally know exactly how large that suspicious file is
      without opening it.

